WEBVTT

00:01:30.560 --> 00:01:34.440
<b>Step 8
"DIY" Means... You Can't Do It? No, I Absolutely Can!</b>

00:01:34.440 --> 00:01:37.060
Here's the extra stuff for today.

00:01:34.440 --> 00:01:37.070
<b>Made by Purin</b>

00:01:34.440 --> 00:01:37.070
<b>Made by Purin</b>

00:01:34.440 --> 00:01:37.070
<b>Made by Purin</b>

00:01:35.570 --> 00:01:37.070
<b>Made by Jobko</b>

00:01:36.450 --> 00:01:37.070
<b>Made by Purin</b>

00:01:37.060 --> 00:01:38.590
Wow!

00:01:38.590 --> 00:01:41.280
Jobko-chan, you always 
bring in amazing stuff!

00:01:41.900 --> 00:01:43.670
Your sense of style is superb!

00:01:44.710 --> 00:01:48.070
W-Well, yes, I guess it is.

00:01:48.540 --> 00:01:50.600
<i>Pudding, good job.</i>

00:01:52.330 --> 00:01:55.010
I brought some that I made, too, meow!

00:01:55.830 --> 00:01:58.260
They're all so intricate.

00:01:58.560 --> 00:02:01.080
That's because I used a 3D printer.

00:02:01.080 --> 00:02:03.250
You have a 3D printer?!

00:02:03.640 --> 00:02:05.840
The one at the school.

00:02:06.150 --> 00:02:08.610
You can just use it without 
asking like that?

00:02:08.800 --> 00:02:12.950
I made sure to ditch security when 
I snuck in, so it'll be fine!

00:02:12.950 --> 00:02:14.160
Like a ninja!

00:02:14.160 --> 00:02:16.620
I don't know how that's "fine."

00:02:17.760 --> 00:02:22.120
U-Um, I brought some things I made, too.

00:02:22.120 --> 00:02:26.570
Oh, what did you make?
 Brooches? Rings? Pendants?

00:02:26.570 --> 00:02:29.970
No... not anything like that.

00:02:34.470 --> 00:02:38.330
I took the aprons we got from 
Waku Waku Wan Wan the other day...

00:02:38.330 --> 00:02:42.960
And I... I thought it would be nice if the
 DIY club had something official to wear.

00:02:46.520 --> 00:02:47.740
Takumin!

00:02:47.740 --> 00:02:50.330
These are really amazing!

00:02:50.330 --> 00:02:51.400
Good job!

00:02:51.400 --> 00:02:54.010
Oh, I'm so glad you like them.

00:02:54.010 --> 00:02:57.070
It makes me so happy, meow! 
I'll treasure it, meow!

00:02:57.170 --> 00:03:00.600
<i>Sunflower Girls</i>

00:02:57.170 --> 00:03:00.600
<i>Sunflower Girls</i>

00:02:57.390 --> 00:02:58.570
This is...

00:02:59.350 --> 00:03:01.410
just like <i>SunGirls</i>...

00:03:02.830 --> 00:03:04.800
Y-Yes!

00:03:04.800 --> 00:03:09.980
I remembered when the girls in the garden 
club all put on their matching aprons!

00:03:09.980 --> 00:03:12.760
And it made me want to try doing it myself!

00:03:13.960 --> 00:03:17.080
Your sentiment has been 
received in its entirety!

00:03:17.080 --> 00:03:18.640
Th-Thank you!

00:03:18.640 --> 00:03:21.520
We won't let the <i>SunGirls</i> beat us.

00:03:21.520 --> 00:03:26.020
We, too, shall be like sunflowers, 
and blossom splendidly!

00:03:26.020 --> 00:03:27.020
Yes!

00:03:28.470 --> 00:03:31.450
I-I'm so sorry. I couldn't help myself.

00:03:33.220 --> 00:03:34.530
Well, then...

00:03:34.530 --> 00:03:37.170
Let's go over our income
 and expenditures today.

00:03:40.250 --> 00:03:43.650
The items we listed online are selling well.

00:03:43.650 --> 00:03:45.780
Wow...

00:03:45.780 --> 00:03:46.620
And...

00:03:46.620 --> 00:03:50.610
The items we had out for sale inside 
Waku Wan are also selling well.

00:03:50.610 --> 00:03:53.540
Oh, this is cute.

00:03:53.840 --> 00:03:56.280
It reminds me of my youth.

00:03:56.580 --> 00:04:00.750
If I wear this, will it make my 
husband's heart flutter a bit?

00:04:00.760 --> 00:04:04.250
<b>Students'</b>

00:04:00.760 --> 00:04:04.250
<b>DIY</b>

00:04:01.430 --> 00:04:04.250
They're incredibly popular with the 
older ladies in the neighborhood.

00:04:04.560 --> 00:04:06.330
Really?

00:04:06.330 --> 00:04:11.590
And so, as of yesterday, we've 
made a total of 40,000 yen.

00:04:11.590 --> 00:04:13.370
Wow!

00:04:13.370 --> 00:04:14.920
That much already?

00:04:14.920 --> 00:04:18.990
The day we can buy the tree 
attachment bolts is nearly here.

00:04:18.990 --> 00:04:21.740
A journey of a thousand miles 
begins with a single step, meow!

00:04:23.660 --> 00:04:26.470
Our secret hideout isn't 
just a dream anymore.

00:04:28.070 --> 00:04:31.620
And so, we should start discussing 
concrete details for the layout and—

00:04:30.360 --> 00:04:31.620
Oh, club leader!

00:04:31.620 --> 00:04:32.490
What is it?

00:04:32.490 --> 00:04:36.490
How many of the things I made have sold?

00:04:37.060 --> 00:04:38.500
Well, it's...

00:04:38.500 --> 00:04:39.450
It's...?

00:04:39.830 --> 00:04:41.110
Um...

00:04:45.450 --> 00:04:47.270
Not a single one sold, huh?

00:04:48.790 --> 00:04:50.400
Not a good job.

00:04:51.180 --> 00:04:52.730
It's...

00:04:52.730 --> 00:04:56.800
It's just, Serufu, the things 
you made, the quality—

00:04:57.440 --> 00:05:00.090
The quirkiness might be 
too much for some people.

00:05:00.990 --> 00:05:02.990
No, I know.

00:05:03.460 --> 00:05:05.810
They're a little crooked...

00:05:05.810 --> 00:05:07.920
a little warped...

00:05:07.920 --> 00:05:10.830
a little of the glue is showing...

00:05:10.830 --> 00:05:11.740
A little?

00:05:13.190 --> 00:05:14.070
And so!

00:05:14.070 --> 00:05:18.890
I would like to proceed with concrete 
details for the plan for the secret hideout.

00:05:18.890 --> 00:05:22.480
You pretended nothing happened and just 
brought the conversation back around, meow.

00:05:22.950 --> 00:05:25.970
S-Serufu-san, it's all right.

00:05:25.970 --> 00:05:28.430
I'm sure they'll still sell.

00:05:28.700 --> 00:05:32.210
Oh, I know! Maybe if we reduce 
the price a little...

00:05:33.270 --> 00:05:34.510
Yeah.

00:05:34.510 --> 00:05:39.020
Thanks for comforting me, Takumin.

00:05:39.850 --> 00:05:43.280
What do we do to make 
progress with the plans?

00:05:43.280 --> 00:05:47.160
We figure out what kind 
of secret base we want to build,

00:05:47.160 --> 00:05:50.280
and then we use that idea
to draw up a blueprint.

00:05:50.670 --> 00:05:53.390
Do you mean drafting?

00:05:54.910 --> 00:05:59.500
In practice, it's something that's created 
according to decisions based on the site,

00:05:59.500 --> 00:06:01.630
but that's something the professionals do.

00:06:01.890 --> 00:06:05.200
It isn't like we're making it to sell,

00:06:05.200 --> 00:06:08.270
so we don't need it to be accurate 
down to the millimeter.

00:06:08.270 --> 00:06:10.680
The size, an understanding 
of the materials needed,

00:06:10.680 --> 00:06:14.970
the order of construction... 
A blueprint will help us determine all of that.

00:06:14.970 --> 00:06:15.930
That's right.

00:06:16.350 --> 00:06:17.230
Oh!

00:06:18.090 --> 00:06:21.860
Um, about the design...

00:06:21.860 --> 00:06:25.140
What do you think about having 
Serufu-san bring everyone's ideas together?

00:06:26.410 --> 00:06:27.740
Me?

00:06:27.740 --> 00:06:32.770
Yes. You're good at drawing pictures, 
so I think you'd be perfect.

00:06:32.770 --> 00:06:35.450
I see. That's true!

00:06:35.450 --> 00:06:37.450
I agree!

00:06:37.450 --> 00:06:42.830
Helping Serufu out since she's got zero 
sales makes you a kind person, Takumin.

00:06:42.830 --> 00:06:46.210
O-Oh, no, that's not what I'm doing!

00:06:46.210 --> 00:06:48.110
What do you think, Serufu-san?

00:06:52.920 --> 00:06:54.960
Yeah! I'll give it my best!

00:06:57.440 --> 00:07:00.590
So, given that we'll have Serufu 
bring the design together,

00:07:01.140 --> 00:07:03.600
what kind of secret hideout 
do we want it to be?

00:07:03.600 --> 00:07:05.210
If you have an opinion, please speak up.

00:07:05.210 --> 00:07:06.390
Please do!

00:07:06.610 --> 00:07:08.730
I want a swing, meow.

00:07:08.730 --> 00:07:11.630
A long one that feels like 
it's hanging from the sky!

00:07:11.630 --> 00:07:14.360
A swing... Sounds nice!

00:07:14.360 --> 00:07:17.690
I'd like to be able to look out 
at the scenery and drink tea.

00:07:18.080 --> 00:07:20.250
Maybe a counter or something by the window?

00:07:20.250 --> 00:07:22.830
A counter... Sounds nice!

00:07:22.830 --> 00:07:25.020
We can't leave out a hammock.

00:07:25.020 --> 00:07:27.620
A hammock... Sounds nice!

00:07:27.620 --> 00:07:31.570
It'd be nice if it had a chimney. 
Just for decoration, of course.

00:07:31.570 --> 00:07:33.970
A chimney... Sounds nice!

00:07:34.250 --> 00:07:38.080
I want to try swinging from a pulley 
on the roof of the secret hideout!

00:07:38.080 --> 00:07:39.400
A pulley...

00:07:39.400 --> 00:07:41.350
What about a skylight?

00:07:41.740 --> 00:07:45.590
That might be nice! Though 
making one might be hard.

00:07:46.140 --> 00:07:47.970
Skylight, skylight...

00:07:47.970 --> 00:07:50.720
We need a drone landing pad.

00:07:50.720 --> 00:07:51.900
Do we?

00:07:51.900 --> 00:07:54.370
Drone, drone...

00:07:54.750 --> 00:07:58.670
We also need a secret revolving door 
and a space to hide a sword, right?

00:07:58.670 --> 00:08:00.380
Are we making a ninja mansion?

00:08:00.380 --> 00:08:02.210
A secret revolving door...

00:08:02.210 --> 00:08:03.010
A space to hide a sword...

00:08:03.010 --> 00:08:04.400
You don't need to write those.

00:08:04.400 --> 00:08:08.080
Oh, yeah! It'd be cool if it 
could transform, right?

00:08:08.080 --> 00:08:10.130
That would be cool, meow!

00:08:10.130 --> 00:08:11.710
Don't get carried away!

00:08:11.710 --> 00:08:13.170
Sorry!

00:08:13.180 --> 00:08:15.430
 Treehouse Design

00:08:13.180 --> 00:08:15.430
Swing

00:08:13.180 --> 00:08:15.430
Counter

00:08:13.180 --> 00:08:15.430
Want to 
drink tea there

00:08:13.180 --> 00:08:15.430
Hammock

00:08:13.180 --> 00:08:15.430
Chimney

00:08:13.180 --> 00:08:15.430
(decorative)

00:08:13.180 --> 00:08:15.430
Swing from a pulley

00:08:13.180 --> 00:08:15.430
Skylight

00:08:13.180 --> 00:08:15.430
Drone

00:08:13.180 --> 00:08:15.430
Secret door   Sword

00:08:13.180 --> 00:08:15.430
Transform

00:08:14.260 --> 00:08:15.430
Okay.

00:08:15.430 --> 00:08:18.360
We have all the ideas everyone 
had in their heads, right?

00:08:18.560 --> 00:08:20.280
Okay!

00:08:20.280 --> 00:08:22.180
I'm all fired up now!

00:08:22.770 --> 00:08:24.870
<i>Is this really going to be okay?</i>

00:08:42.060 --> 00:08:44.250
It's done!

00:08:44.250 --> 00:08:46.830
Concept art for our secret hideout!

00:08:51.010 --> 00:08:52.460
This is...

00:08:52.750 --> 00:08:54.720
You drew this in one night?

00:08:55.060 --> 00:08:58.000
Lots of different ideas 
bubbled up inside me...

00:08:58.000 --> 00:09:00.220
Serufucchi, you're amazing!

00:09:00.220 --> 00:09:01.810
This house...

00:09:02.340 --> 00:09:04.710
is flying through space, right?

00:09:04.710 --> 00:09:07.100
Lots of different ideas 
bubbled up inside me...

00:09:07.530 --> 00:09:09.690
This tree house...

00:09:09.690 --> 00:09:12.940
is more of a tree town.

00:09:12.940 --> 00:09:15.200
Lots of different ideas 
bubbled up inside me!

00:09:17.020 --> 00:09:21.070
There are roller coasters and even 
Ferris wheels throughout the tree!

00:09:21.070 --> 00:09:23.450
Lots of different ideas 
bubbled up inside me!

00:09:23.450 --> 00:09:25.370
Wow!

00:09:25.370 --> 00:09:29.450
There's even a tree house 
inside the tree trunk!

00:09:29.450 --> 00:09:31.950
Lots of different ideas 
bubbled up inside me!

00:09:32.260 --> 00:09:37.920
Um, Serufu-san, your 
illustration is truly lovely...

00:09:37.920 --> 00:09:43.390
but I think using this illustration to 
build... might be a little difficult.

00:09:43.390 --> 00:09:45.940
Yeah. That's true.

00:09:45.940 --> 00:09:47.610
B-But, you know...

00:09:47.950 --> 00:09:51.450
I really love the shape of 
this roof and chimney...

00:09:51.450 --> 00:09:54.940
and the feel of this window.

00:09:54.940 --> 00:09:59.690
So, we could pull out each of the good points
 and the things we think we can build,

00:10:00.190 --> 00:10:02.950
then combine them together. 
What do you think?

00:10:03.230 --> 00:10:05.950
I see. That's true.

00:10:05.950 --> 00:10:09.030
We can't make a rocket tree house,

00:10:09.030 --> 00:10:12.140
but I think we could make a tire swing!

00:10:12.140 --> 00:10:13.790
Oh!

00:10:14.620 --> 00:10:16.820
And this pulley slide that 
connects two planets...

00:10:16.820 --> 00:10:20.540
could connect the tree house 
and club room roofs instead.

00:10:20.540 --> 00:10:21.830
I see!

00:10:22.240 --> 00:10:25.100
Even if a drone landing pad 
is difficult to fit in,

00:10:25.100 --> 00:10:27.710
you did a good job on this hammock!

00:10:27.710 --> 00:10:29.350
Jobko-chan!

00:10:29.350 --> 00:10:30.510
Okay!

00:10:30.510 --> 00:10:33.530
Let's all compile pieces from 
Serufu's illustration together!

00:10:33.530 --> 00:10:34.610
Yes!

00:10:33.530 --> 00:10:34.610
Meow!

00:10:37.650 --> 00:10:41.660
<b>DIY Club</b>

00:10:42.510 --> 00:10:43.910
It's done!

00:10:43.910 --> 00:10:47.910
<b>DIY Club</b>

00:10:48.150 --> 00:10:49.460
Looks good.

00:10:49.460 --> 00:10:50.980
Serufucchi, nice work!

00:10:53.400 --> 00:10:56.830
It will become a wonderful 
symbol of the DIY club!

00:10:56.830 --> 00:10:58.240
Wow!

00:10:58.710 --> 00:11:02.170
I suddenly have an overwhelming 
feeling that we can build this!

00:11:02.170 --> 00:11:07.420
So, who is going to use this 
illustration to draft a blueprint?

00:11:09.220 --> 00:11:10.270
What?

00:11:23.700 --> 00:11:28.450
<b>DIY Club</b>

00:11:25.150 --> 00:11:28.450
This looks like it's going to 
become something wonderful.

00:11:28.450 --> 00:11:31.110
Serufu-san, it's very good.

00:11:33.110 --> 00:11:35.910
So, how will you make the blueprint?

00:11:35.910 --> 00:11:41.710
I've done rough blueprints for things 
like shelves and chairs before,

00:11:41.710 --> 00:11:45.230
but never for something as big 
as this secret hideout...

00:11:45.230 --> 00:11:49.300
It needs to be really well done, right?

00:11:49.300 --> 00:11:52.360
Yes, that's true.

00:11:52.360 --> 00:11:57.130
Even for AI, making a blueprint from an 
illustration would probably be impossible.

00:11:57.130 --> 00:12:00.350
It'd be helpful for strength tests 
and simulating colors, but...

00:12:01.940 --> 00:12:03.200
I know!

00:12:03.590 --> 00:12:04.990
Know what?

00:12:04.990 --> 00:12:07.480
I'll draft the blueprint!

00:12:07.480 --> 00:12:08.760
What?!

00:12:08.760 --> 00:12:11.010
A blueprint would probably 
be a little too...

00:12:11.010 --> 00:12:12.250
Just a little...

00:12:14.370 --> 00:12:18.440
All right. It'll be hard, but I'll 
work hard to figure it out somehow—

00:12:18.440 --> 00:12:19.960
I'll do it.

00:12:19.960 --> 00:12:20.730
What?

00:12:21.640 --> 00:12:23.250
Jobko-chan?

00:12:23.250 --> 00:12:24.790
Can you do it?

00:12:26.060 --> 00:12:27.690
Yes, I can.

00:12:27.690 --> 00:12:31.680
A blueprint. That's easier 
than eating breakfast.

00:12:32.200 --> 00:12:35.620
Then you could have said 
something yesterday.

00:12:35.620 --> 00:12:39.330
Sorry. I just wanted to see 
how things went, that's all.

00:12:49.480 --> 00:12:51.990
Measuring the tree that 
will serve as the base...

00:12:53.120 --> 00:12:54.390
Measurements complete.

00:12:55.840 --> 00:12:59.060
I'll use this data to create the blueprint.

00:12:59.760 --> 00:13:02.010
Jobko-san, you're so dependable!

00:13:02.010 --> 00:13:04.160
All our hopes are pinned on you, meow!

00:13:04.160 --> 00:13:05.980
We really can leave it to you, right?

00:13:05.980 --> 00:13:07.470
Of course!

00:13:07.470 --> 00:13:10.180
Consider yourselves to be in safe hands.

00:13:14.430 --> 00:13:17.430
I tried making our curry 
tonight with chicken.

00:13:20.770 --> 00:13:23.600
It's a little spicy, but it's delicious!

00:13:23.600 --> 00:13:25.120
I'm so glad.

00:13:25.120 --> 00:13:27.600
Maybe tomorrow we'll turn 
it into katsu curry.

00:13:30.720 --> 00:13:34.720
To think she can draft blueprints... 
That's a girl genius for you!

00:13:34.720 --> 00:13:36.680
She can do anything!

00:13:36.680 --> 00:13:37.510
Yeah.

00:13:37.510 --> 00:13:40.750
Takumi's really good at detailed work.

00:13:40.750 --> 00:13:43.380
Our club leader can make anything.

00:13:43.380 --> 00:13:46.460
Shii-chan is nimble and strong.

00:13:46.460 --> 00:13:50.140
Everyone in the DIY club is really amazing.

00:13:50.140 --> 00:13:53.210
I wish I could be more 
helpful to all of them!

00:13:53.210 --> 00:13:56.090
But you drew the illustration, didn't you?

00:13:56.090 --> 00:13:57.760
Yes, but...

00:13:58.220 --> 00:14:02.040
The brooches I made aren't selling... 
and if things keep going this way,

00:14:02.040 --> 00:14:06.800
I don't know what I'll be able to do when 
we actually build our secret hideout.

00:14:08.730 --> 00:14:09.850
Okay!

00:14:09.850 --> 00:14:10.850
Mother!

00:14:10.850 --> 00:14:12.820
The hammer and saw and screwdrivers...

00:14:12.820 --> 00:14:15.720
and all the other tools! 
Where did we put them?

00:14:16.550 --> 00:14:17.310
What?

00:14:26.220 --> 00:14:27.370
What's that?

00:14:27.370 --> 00:14:28.740
Whoops!

00:14:30.310 --> 00:14:32.810
Is she pounding in nails or something?

00:14:32.810 --> 00:14:34.690
I hope she doesn't hurt herself.

00:14:34.690 --> 00:14:35.720
Ow!

00:14:39.440 --> 00:14:41.200
Jobko-chan?

00:14:41.200 --> 00:14:42.820
Did you take a bath?

00:14:46.240 --> 00:14:47.700
What's wrong?

00:14:47.700 --> 00:14:49.250
Do you have a stomachache?

00:14:53.490 --> 00:14:55.090
Those are...

00:14:55.370 --> 00:14:57.040
What are those blueprints for?

00:14:59.020 --> 00:15:01.820
Um... Jobko-chan?

00:15:06.650 --> 00:15:09.340
Then, I'm going to take a bath first, okay?

00:15:17.580 --> 00:15:20.980
<i>I wonder what Serufu is trying to make.</i>

00:15:22.780 --> 00:15:25.220
That sea glass I picked up the other day...

00:15:25.220 --> 00:15:27.120
Maybe I'll make it into a bracelet.

00:15:27.740 --> 00:15:29.890
I'll use a router to drill the holes...

00:15:29.890 --> 00:15:31.650
pass a chain through it...

00:15:31.650 --> 00:15:35.180
Wait! This is no time to be 
thinking about things like that!

00:15:36.130 --> 00:15:38.260
I have to make progress on my assignment!

00:15:43.050 --> 00:15:44.410
Jobko-chan?

00:15:57.300 --> 00:16:00.900
<i>Could it be that she wants to 
talk something over with me?</i>

00:16:01.170 --> 00:16:05.650
Jobko-chan, it seemed like you were 
worrying over something earlier.

00:16:06.800 --> 00:16:08.630
Was it those blueprints?

00:16:08.630 --> 00:16:10.720
They looked pretty old.

00:16:14.880 --> 00:16:18.690
If it isn't a bother, would 
you tell me all about it?

00:16:19.800 --> 00:16:22.050
I suppose I have no choice.

00:16:22.050 --> 00:16:27.720
If you want to know that badly, Pudding, 
then I suppose I could tell you.

00:16:31.330 --> 00:16:37.730
Those are blueprints for a treehouse 
that my mom drafted when I was little.

00:16:37.730 --> 00:16:39.960
Really? Your mama...

00:16:39.960 --> 00:16:41.910
My treasure!

00:16:41.910 --> 00:16:43.940
Why were you looking at them?

00:16:44.500 --> 00:16:47.570
It has been decided that
 I will draft the blueprints

00:16:47.570 --> 00:16:50.940
for the DIY club's secret hideout.

00:16:50.940 --> 00:16:52.640
That's amazing!

00:16:53.240 --> 00:16:55.210
Not really.

00:16:55.210 --> 00:16:59.590
I was worried about leaving it to any 
of the others, so I took it on myself.

00:16:59.590 --> 00:17:03.820
So then you thought you'd use your 
mama's blueprints as a reference?

00:17:03.820 --> 00:17:04.900
Something like that.

00:17:05.190 --> 00:17:06.930
Did they help?

00:17:07.850 --> 00:17:09.890
I don't know.

00:17:09.890 --> 00:17:10.600
What?

00:17:11.860 --> 00:17:13.600
I don't have any idea.

00:17:14.150 --> 00:17:16.300
What do you mean?

00:17:16.300 --> 00:17:19.930
I mean, I've never studied blueprints.

00:17:19.930 --> 00:17:22.230
I don't know anything about architecture.

00:17:22.230 --> 00:17:25.580
I don't even know how to use CAD for things.

00:17:25.580 --> 00:17:27.710
Jobko-chan, you're a genius.

00:17:27.710 --> 00:17:29.680
You can learn to do it 
in no time, can't you?

00:17:29.680 --> 00:17:32.220
That's right. I'm a genius.

00:17:32.220 --> 00:17:34.390
I can do whatever I try to do.

00:17:35.000 --> 00:17:36.270
But, you know...

00:17:36.790 --> 00:17:40.920
There's just not enough time 
to start studying from zero!

00:17:42.340 --> 00:17:46.030
Then why did you take it 
on in the first place?

00:17:46.030 --> 00:17:48.720
Well... it's...

00:17:48.720 --> 00:17:49.790
It's...?

00:17:51.080 --> 00:17:53.040
Because it was fun.

00:17:53.920 --> 00:17:57.930
Because it was so much fun back then!

00:17:58.710 --> 00:18:02.240
Building a tree house with mom.

00:18:02.240 --> 00:18:04.850
I worked as hard as I could to help.

00:18:05.300 --> 00:18:07.530
Papa was happy, too.

00:18:10.230 --> 00:18:13.820
Serufu, our club leader, 
Takumin, and Shii...

00:18:13.820 --> 00:18:16.880
If they all felt that same way, then...

00:18:16.880 --> 00:18:18.850
I thought it'd be nice.

00:18:18.850 --> 00:18:22.230
When do you need the blueprints by?

00:18:22.230 --> 00:18:25.110
We wan' t'ave th' secr't h'deout 
don' b'summer vac'tion.

00:18:25.110 --> 00:18:25.750
What?

00:18:26.270 --> 00:18:29.920
We were saying that we wanted to 
start right after the rainy season,

00:18:29.920 --> 00:18:31.740
so by the end of this month.

00:18:32.350 --> 00:18:34.210
That means you have less than ten days!

00:18:34.480 --> 00:18:38.300
I'm only here for the first term,

00:18:38.300 --> 00:18:40.800
so I want it to be finished 
within that time.

00:18:43.910 --> 00:18:45.750
All right.

00:18:45.750 --> 00:18:47.510
I'll help you.

00:18:47.510 --> 00:18:48.740
You can do that?

00:18:48.970 --> 00:18:51.320
I've never drafted blueprints either,

00:18:51.320 --> 00:18:54.370
but if there are two of us,
 it should take half the time, right?

00:18:57.210 --> 00:18:59.030
I love you, Pudding!

00:18:59.030 --> 00:19:02.130
Wha?! Hey! Don't touch me in weird places!

00:19:02.130 --> 00:19:05.540
It's all right! Don't worry about it!

