<b>Kanegi Fruits Village</b>

00:19:15.250 --> 00:19:17.670
Mango 
<b>750 yen</b>

00:19:15.250 --> 00:19:17.670
Strawberry 
<b>500 yen</b>

00:19:15.250 --> 00:19:17.670
Shine Muscat 
<b>500 yen</b>

00:19:17.670 --> 00:19:20.680
<b>Kanegi Fruits Village</b>

00:19:31.230 --> 00:19:33.610
<b>Anyone Can Do It</b>

00:19:31.230 --> 00:19:33.610
<b>An Easy Primer</b>

00:19:38.360 --> 00:19:40.610
Tree Climbing

00:19:38.360 --> 00:19:40.610
<b>Captain Matsuda</b>

00:20:21.870 --> 00:20:23.230
Good morning,

00:20:23.230 --> 00:20:24.670
Jobko-chan.

00:20:24.670 --> 00:20:26.150
Good morning.

00:20:27.710 --> 00:20:29.440
Hey, Pudding?

00:20:29.440 --> 00:20:30.630
What is it?

00:20:31.080 --> 00:20:32.990
Just...

00:20:32.990 --> 00:20:36.880
Thank you. It's because of you that 
I managed to finish the blueprints.

00:20:36.880 --> 00:20:40.670
I... had a lot of fun, too!

00:20:41.000 --> 00:20:45.490
I know that everyone in the DIY club 
will be grateful to you, too.

00:20:45.490 --> 00:20:49.850
K-Keep it a secret that I helped, okay?

00:20:49.850 --> 00:20:51.110
Why?

00:20:51.110 --> 00:20:56.990
I mean, I said that DIY was 
moldy and behind the times.

00:20:56.990 --> 00:20:59.180
I made fun of it so much...

00:20:59.180 --> 00:21:00.660
To say otherwise now...

00:21:00.660 --> 00:21:03.010
Yeah, I guess that's true.

00:21:03.010 --> 00:21:04.460
Still...

00:21:04.460 --> 00:21:07.120
Summer in Japan is muggy!

00:21:07.120 --> 00:21:09.660
The rainy season and summer 
are both pretty awful.

00:21:11.040 --> 00:21:13.990
Jobko-chan, you're incredible!

00:21:13.990 --> 00:21:16.030
That's a girl genius for you!

00:21:16.030 --> 00:21:17.220
They're spectacular.

00:21:17.220 --> 00:21:19.300
The definition of a "good job," meow!

00:21:19.300 --> 00:21:21.320
With these, everything should be just fine.

00:21:21.320 --> 00:21:23.830
I take my hat off to you, Jobko-san!

00:21:24.670 --> 00:21:28.340
Well, if I turn my hand to 
something like this, it's easy!

00:21:28.340 --> 00:21:33.000
It's likely that as you're working,
 you'll find things that need to be altered,

00:21:33.000 --> 00:21:35.010
but let's leave that for when it happens.

00:21:35.010 --> 00:21:37.730
We have most of the materials 
and the funds now, too.

00:21:37.730 --> 00:21:39.660
The rainy season's over.

00:21:39.660 --> 00:21:43.820
When we're done with our midterms, 
let's start working on our secret hideout!

00:21:43.820 --> 00:21:45.640
Yes, ma'am!

00:21:43.820 --> 00:21:45.640
Okay!

00:21:45.640 --> 00:21:47.560
Work hard, all right?

00:21:47.560 --> 00:21:48.530
Oh, right!

00:21:49.610 --> 00:21:51.140
The thing is...

00:21:51.140 --> 00:21:53.830
Before we start building the secret hideout,

00:21:53.830 --> 00:21:57.740
I'd like to have the whole club
 over to my house.

00:21:57.740 --> 00:21:59.610
To your house, Serufucchi?

00:21:59.610 --> 00:22:00.590
Why?

00:22:01.500 --> 00:22:04.110
There's something I want you to see!

00:23:36.140 --> 00:23:39.930
<b>Step 9</b>

00:23:36.140 --> 00:23:39.930
<b>Does "DIY" Mean a Shocking Surprise? 
How Unexpected! So It's Really Unexpected!</b>
